% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/plan_types.py` as the Pure stdlib shared types, no I/O and no imports outside the standard library. Frozen dataclasses PlanMeta, PlanPaths, Rev, Bunch, OrderConstraints, TransitionOverride, EffectiveNote. PlanStatus is a StrEnum of exactly wip|ready|archived ('wip' is PRD-sourced from 'work in progress'; 'ready' and 'archived' are design-sourced and must not be back-attributed to the PRD). Author is a StrEnum of human|agent|llm ('llm' is PRD-sourced from 'work with an LLM'). Actor is a StrEnum of gui|cli|agent and is a DISTINCT type from Author that must never be merged despite both containing 'agent': actor is which surface issued the write, author is who composed the content, so an LLM driving the CLI is actor=cli, author=llm and collapsing them makes that case unrepresentable. TransitionOverride fields: from_track_id, to_track_id, technique?, beats?, showcase_move?, effects?, note?, author?, state (active|orphaned); author is optional so records written before the field existed round-trip as None rather than raising. PlanPaths has exactly 10 members: root, plan_json, selection, exclusions, playlist, mix_plan, notes, bunches, transitions, journal. slugify() NFKD-normalizes then reduces to a lowercase kebab slug; validate_slug() raises on anything else; header_safe() strips CR/LF because http.server's send_header does not validate them and display_name is free-form user text. RESERVED_SLUGS = {'active','trash'} plus a leading-dot rule: slugify('Active') must NOT return 'active' but route through the same -2/-3 collision path as a duplicate name, because a slug of 'active' collides with both the /api/plans/active route and plan_paths.resolve()'s active.json read.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

Pure stdlib shared types, no I/O and no imports outside the standard library. Frozen dataclasses PlanMeta, PlanPaths, Rev, Bunch, OrderConstraints, TransitionOverride, EffectiveNote. PlanStatus is a StrEnum of exactly wip|ready|archived ('wip' is PRD-sourced from 'work in progress'; 'ready' and 'archived' are design-sourced and must not be back-attributed to the PRD). Author is a StrEnum of human|agent|llm ('llm' is PRD-sourced from 'work with an LLM'). Actor is a StrEnum of gui|cli|agent and is a DISTINCT type from Author that must never be merged despite both containing 'agent': actor is which surface issued the write, author is who composed the content, so an LLM driving the CLI is actor=cli, author=llm and collapsing them makes that case unrepresentable. TransitionOverride fields: from_track_id, to_track_id, technique?, beats?, showcase_move?, effects?, note?, author?, state (active|orphaned); author is optional so records written before the field existed round-trip as None rather than raising. PlanPaths has exactly 10 members: root, plan_json, selection, exclusions, playlist, mix_plan, notes, bunches, transitions, journal. slugify() NFKD-normalizes then reduces to a lowercase kebab slug; validate_slug() raises on anything else; header_safe() strips CR/LF because http.server's send_header does not validate them and display_name is free-form user text. RESERVED_SLUGS = {'active','trash'} plus a leading-dot rule: slugify('Active') must NOT return 'active' but route through the same -2/-3 collision path as a duplicate name, because a slug of 'active' collides with both the /api/plans/active route and plan_paths.resolve()'s active.json read.

